{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion","id":592883,"title":"What are the worst Classic WoD sourcebooks, in your opinion?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-16T10:17:03-07:00","id":592883,"title":"What are the worst Classic WoD sourcebooks, in your opinion?","content":"I really like the old World of Darkness in general, but I know that not every book they've put out is gold. However, sometimes, I really enjoy reading terrible things. So I'm looking for recommendations, basically. I'd love to know what your least favorite classic WoD sourcebooks are and why, so that I can try to find them, read them, and suffer myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T10:27:32-07:00","id":592901,"title":"","content":"Say it with me here kids:<br /> <br /> 3..<br /> <br /> 2...<br /> <br /> 1....<br /> <br /> <b><i><span style=\"font-size:18px\">GYPSIES.</span></i></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T10:57:16-07:00","id":592915,"title":"","content":"+1. Gypsies.<br /> Followed closely by the Revised Tribe book Children of Gaia. There us an entire thread on this book on The Werewolf forym","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T11:06:05-07:00","id":592934,"title":"","content":"The Blood-Dimmed Tides was pretty subpar.<br /> EDIT: I take it back. I've been re-reading Blood-Dimmed Tides, and actually really liking it.<br /> <br /> You might want to read Shadows of Iceland!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6883,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","user":"DarkExcalibur42","date":". 07-16-2015, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T11:18:41-07:00","id":592953,"title":"","content":"+1 Gypsies.<br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb, one of the major problems with White Wolf was allways that they just reproduced a lot of common american prejudice when talking about the world outside North America. It wasn't ill intended as far as I know, and it got better with time, but not so much. They mostly know near to nothing about how the world really is.<br /> <br /> But it never, ever, was so awfully made as in Gypsies. That piece of crap is so bad that I found better to look for D&amp;D's Ravenloft source books on the Vistani instead. And it is pretty bad already if taken out of context. Heck, the guy that recomended to me to use the Vistani instead IS a gypsy...<br /> <br /> That aside, I can't remember right now another book that struck me so badly. Hunter X, maybe. I find it just too weird, and absolutely against the feeling of the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T11:26:25-07:00","id":592958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=592953#post592953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">D&amp;D's Ravenloft source books on the Vistani instead. And it is pretty bad already if taken out of context.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Vistani are pretty badass! I really like their backstory and character in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That aside, I can't remember right now another book that struck me so badly. Hunter X, maybe. I find it just too weird, and absolutely against the feeling of the World of Darkness. </div> </div> </div>You can't really judge Demon Hunter X in comparison to the rest of the World of Darkness. It's part of the Kindred of the East and all that jazz, and purposely took a higher action-oriented angle.<br /> <br /> Demon Hunter X lets you play an anime about fighting monsters. And it does a pretty good job of that. It's a great source book, but has limited use. The Shih have wider potential use in the WoD as a whole than do the Strike Force Zero agents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T12:35:38-07:00","id":593014,"title":"","content":"WOD: Gypsies takes a well deserved top billing here.<br /> <br /> Kindred of the East and a lot of the related Year of the Lotus books aren't great. They're not the worst really, but there's serious issues (really just see the multiple threads about a possible KotE20 already on here)<br /> <br /> The 1e/2e Tribe and Tradition books are pretty bad. You could easily rename most of them &quot;How to Make Insulting Ethnic/Cultural Stereotypes a Bigger Part of Your Games, Part X.&quot; Most of the Revised versions of these books managed to undo a lot of the damage here. This actually makes the highly disliked Revised ones worse in how much people react to them. Celestial Chorus Revised really isn't that bad, but it's so below the bar set by some of the other Revised Tradition books and doesn't really do much about some of the issues in the previous edition material, that it was more poorly received that it would be in a vacuum. Children of Gaia Revised is probably the worst of these since it went a step farther and got worse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T12:52:56-07:00","id":593063,"title":"","content":"Let's give a nod to Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T13:19:10-07:00","id":593098,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/62512/Shadows-of-Iceland?term=shadows+of+iceland&amp;manufacturers_id=1\" target=\"_blank\">Shadows of Iceland</a> was purposely bad, being an April Fool's joke. I really enjoyed reading that, and the OP did say she was looking for something bad to enjoy reading ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6883,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","user":"DarkExcalibur42","date":". 07-16-2015, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T13:34:23-07:00","id":593104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkExcalibur42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=593098#post593098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/62512/Shadows-of-Iceland?term=shadows+of+iceland&amp;manufacturers_id=1\" target=\"_blank\">Shadows of Iceland</a> was purposely bad, being an April Fool's joke. I really enjoyed reading that, and the OP did say he was looking for something bad to enjoy reading ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>As was Fargo By Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T13:37:51-07:00","id":593106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=592953#post592953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That aside, I can't remember right now another book that struck me so badly. Hunter X, maybe. I find it just too weird, and absolutely against the feeling of the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage did everything in that book before it showed up. Werewolf is pretty high actiony too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T13:41:11-07:00","id":593107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkExcalibur42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=593098#post593098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/62512/Shadows-of-Iceland?term=shadows+of+iceland&amp;manufacturers_id=1\" target=\"_blank\">Shadows of Iceland</a> was purposely bad, being an April Fool's joke. I really enjoyed reading that, and the OP did say he was looking for something bad to enjoy reading ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> She, actually. :-)<br /> <br /> I appreciate any recommendations of terrible books, whether they're intentionally or unintentionally bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T14:32:04-07:00","id":593154,"title":"","content":"Gypsies, that sound interesting.<br /> I really curious about American prejudice point of view on them. Especially because I live in central Europe (many gypsies live here) and therefore i have some experience with them or know people who have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5536-arkilijo","name":"Arkilijo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T15:08:19-07:00","id":593202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=593107#post593107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> She, actually. :-)<br /> <br /> I appreciate any recommendations of terrible books, whether they're intentionally or unintentionally bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Old internet habit of mine, defaulting to male pronouns. My mistake!<br /> <br /> And everything I know about Gypsies, I learned from listening to Gogol Bordello ^_^<br /> <br /> So admittedly, it's basically nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T16:51:15-07:00","id":593328,"title":"","content":"Childen of Gaia revised. Just, that.<br /> <br /> Rage Across Australia. Poor NPCs, characters that don't obey the rules of the setting,etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T17:40:22-07:00","id":593395,"title":"","content":"The original Clanbook: Malkavian tops my list because of what it did to that clan as a whole. Gypsies didn't bother me much because nobody in my troupe had any intention of playing a Gypsy. DSotBH is a guilty pleasure. Rage Across Australia is definitely a close number two, and Tribebook: Child of Gaia revised wasn't interesting to me.<br /> <br /> But man, that Malkavian book.<br /> <br /> First, I am still not sure to this day what the goal was with the layout. To make us all think we got defective books, maybe? And the Malkavian Madness Network, gawd!! And of course, the book led to a marked increase in fishmalks. After paying real monies for that book back in the day, I almost lost confidence in White Wolf. It is still my most pristine WoD book, sitting untouched on a shelf except when I need to show someone a physical representation of my anger.<br /> <br /> F that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T17:49:52-07:00","id":593398,"title":"","content":"Demon Hunter X only makes sense in the context of the Year of the Lotus material.<br /> <br /> And to think about that, I would throw most of those books on the garbage. I don't feel they add to the WoD setting, except to make the default western setting looks like shit.<br /> <br /> Nothing against its feeling by itself. But to me is like treating Street Fighter RPG as a part of the core WoD setting...<br /> <br /> But for sure, nothing there is worse than Gypsy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T19:31:19-07:00","id":593470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=593398#post593398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon Hunter X only makes sense in the context of the Year of the Lotus material.<br /> <br /> And to think about that, I would throw most of those books on the garbage. I don't feel they add to the WoD setting, except to make the default western setting looks like shit.<br /> <br /> Nothing against its feeling by itself. But to me is like treating Street Fighter RPG as a part of the core WoD setting...</div> </div> </div> </div>Shih and SF0 were both actually written as being like side-franchises of Mage, and they're much more low-key than the parent material in Mage that produces zeppelins flying out of the atmosphere and engaging in battles around the moons of Jupiter with ultratech battlecruisers sent out from a secret cabal's Dyson sphere far away from the Earth. Mage is like the emporium of genre-breaking material, as far as the rest of the games are concerned. Horror can often have just beyond the cutting edge stuff, but everything that the Technocracy and Traditions were throwing around is just... urgh. I didn't sign up for that when I tentatively passed by Vampire or picked up Werewolf. Even being kept off-camera, it's still incredibly genre-dissonant for a modern game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T20:38:39-07:00","id":593495,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm usually not a fan of anything to do with Mage...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T00:52:23-07:00","id":593623,"title":"","content":"Yes, Mage do a lot of genre-breaking. In the scope of the line, it doesn't bother me. At least, it doesn't hurt so much the other lines. Tremere was a Mage, so what? No stablished theme of the setting was broken, because Mage doesn't assume to deal a lot with the others.<br /> <br /> But the East As Kung Fu material? First, it did an entire hemisphere, and in fact the one with MOST people, just be barred to anything stablished by the other lines. Caine was one of the first humans and the first vampires, but somehow not even a single vamp can live in the East because a bunch of Super-Kung-Fu-Undead wih Blessed souls hate vampires. Gaia is dying because the Fera are few in number, scatered, paranoid, and the werewolfs can't work together well enough with their Rage, except in the East the Fera have an Emerald Court where everyone works together and form miscelaneous war parties, some of them with spiritual Zords. The Technocracy is turning the world into a sterile Consensus of Stasis, but they have no hold in the East, where the NWO was fooled by five chinese traditions based on ancient religion and confucionism.<br /> <br /> The world is shrouded in shadows, the common people absolutely ignorant of the monsters around them. Excet by the fact that two thirds of human population lives in a hemisphere where no one really gives a damn if the delivery guy turns into a half-tiger cyborg when trouble comes. If he ever becomes a problem himself, our hunters are Kung Fu masters with Hadouken and mecha-warriors.<br /> <br /> Each and every cWoD game line was tainted by this shit! In the East everyone uses completely different rules, the gods know why, everyone is wiser than you, more badass than you, and for some reason YOUR problems are getting huge enough to damn the world...<br /> <br /> Just... just doesn't make any, I mean, absolutely any sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T01:48:25-07:00","id":593636,"title":"","content":"Gypsy was the worst BY far and it was even close. A very very distant second to DSotBH.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T02:15:33-07:00","id":593645,"title":"","content":"G*psies takes it.<br /> <br /> I still can't decide if Montreal by Night was a masterpiece or a screaming trainwreck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T03:46:54-07:00","id":593703,"title":"","content":"Gypsies is obviously number one for me for obvious reasons<br /> <br /> Other picks for me as well as my reasons for selecting them include...<br /> <br /> Kindred of the East (While not as racist as Gypsies, it comes in pretty damn close for me)<br /> <br /> Demon: The Fallen (It's as offensive from a religious perspective as Gypsies and KOTE is from a racial and cultural one)<br /> <br /> Time of Thin Blood (I don't like metaplot, so it ranks low for me. Plus if memory serves me correct, this is when they kill off the Ravnos, which sucks because I like them a lot. Dark Ages and early Revised really redeemed that clan/ And even 2e Ravnos are nowhere near as offensive as the very concept of Kuei-Jin in my opinion)<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia Tribebook Revised (Well, any of the Revised Clanbooks and Tribebooks rank low for me, due to the aforementioned metaplot. This one just stands out more and sucks for other non-metaplot reasons)<br /> <br /> Any of the Time of Judgment books (Gehenna, etc. Not really a fan of torching your own setting, though the metaplot and some poor choices in the initial game designs in 1e are to blame for these books. That and it was the 90s, so pre-millennial apocalyptic stuff was quite trendy then )<br /> <br /> New York By Night (Too railroady and metaplot-heavy in my opinion)<br /> <br /> Berlin By Night (Two words. Heinrich Himmler. That is all)<br /> <br /> Clanbook: Baali (Ewww.....)<br /> <br /> Charnel Houses of Europe: The Shoah (I understand that White Wolf did their best to be respectful to the subject material, and while it does retcon Berlin by Night, there are still certain subjects that RPG publishers, especially ones with the mixed history White Wolf in the 90's had, should not touch with a ten-foot pole. The Holocaust is one of these subjects. I'm sure the book itself is probably good from what I have heard, but the idea of it makes me very uncomfortable)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, I am actually kind of fine with Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand. It's not great, but it's not THAT bad either. At this point, I think it's so widely hated these days is because it's trendy to hate it. I mean, as weird as Soul Eaters are, it's a hell of a lot better than Gypsies, Demon: The Fallen, Vampire Nazis, or torching your own setting and then running like hell. Compared to the books I just mentioned, Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand is more &quot;meh&quot; than outright bad, at least to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T07:56:16-07:00","id":593792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=593623#post593623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Mage do a lot of genre-breaking. In the scope of the line, it doesn't bother me. At least, it doesn't hurt so much the other lines. Tremere was a Mage, so what? No stablished theme of the setting was broken, because Mage doesn't assume to deal a lot with the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that Mage, with its label ostensibly under the classic WoD, really ruined expectations of what games would entail. It could only really fly if it were a setting unto itself, with no connection to the others. No other game uses the consensus, or thinks of technology as a form of magick, spelled with a special k.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the East As Kung Fu material? First, it did an entire hemisphere, and in fact the one with MOST people, just be barred to anything stablished by the other lines. Caine was one of the first humans and the first vampires, but somehow not even a single vamp can live in the East because a bunch of Super-Kung-Fu-Undead wih Blessed souls hate vampires. Gaia is dying because the Fera are few in number, scatered, paranoid, and the werewolfs can't work together well enough with their Rage, except in the East the Fera have an Emerald Court where everyone works together and form miscelaneous war parties, some of them with spiritual Zords. The Technocracy is turning the world into a sterile Consensus of Stasis, but they have no hold in the East, where the NWO was fooled by five chinese traditions based on ancient religion and confucionism. </div> </div> </div>The Beast Courts actually had this thing called the War of Shame (completely wiped out the Gurahl, which Gurahl elsewhere avoided even in Garou-thick territory), and if you read the stereotypes of each breed to the others, are far from a completely harmonious ideal synthetic family. I'm also not sure where you're getting the notion that they have giant robots, even in spirit; they don't tend to follow Clashing Boom-Boom like the Glass Walkers of the Garou Nation, and the only thing even close to mecha (clumsy exoskeletons at that) comes courtesy of the Book of the Weaver.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The world is shrouded in shadows, the common people absolutely ignorant of the monsters around them. Excet by the fact that two thirds of human population lives in a hemisphere where no one really gives a damn if the delivery guy turns into a half-tiger cyborg when trouble comes. If he ever becomes a problem himself, our hunters are Kung Fu masters with Hadouken and mecha-warriors.<br /> <br /> Each and every cWoD game line was tainted by this shit! In the East everyone uses completely different rules, the gods know why, everyone is wiser than you, more badass than you, and for some reason YOUR problems are getting huge enough to damn the world...<br /> <br /> Just... just doesn't make any, I mean, absolutely any sense. </div> </div> </div>These accusations are bullshit. You're going way off the track of what was actually in the books. Shih are gritty, scarred martial artist knights-errant that have a very small bag of tricks not even even close to Street Fighter (no wave-motion fists, no dragon punches, nothing of the sort). Strike Force Zero had personnel with a limited number of advanced prosthetics. As for mecha, they're likely all to be found in &quot;main-line&quot; Mage, under the aegis of the Technocracy. Score another one for Mage, which, like Werewolf, didn't have any actual different rules differences between &quot;main-line&quot; and YotL material (groups of five are conveniently what you also get in Garou packs). All the Garou and Fera and willworkers used exactly the same rules no matter where they were, and the paradigm of death in the Dark Kingdom of Jade was quite close to that of Stygia, so there were maybe a slight number of Arcanoi that were different between the two (no Castigation, very rarely you would get Inhabit).<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Given the atmosphere presented in DHX (you're a scarred lone demon hunter who's kind of falling apart or a justifiably paranoid and scared secret agent with a few odd medical implants that only sort of mollify the tremendous gulf between you and the monsters), it's really not too out of place. Which, again, is more than can be said for having Hogwarts on Mars fighting off spaceships that are in the spirit world because whaaaaaaaat? Much more down to earth, in a very literal sense. Besides, KotE already mentioned that most monster hunters of a religious bent would still be using the same True Faith rules, so the only thing missing there is emphasizing that more people use True Faith, psychic powers and sorcery than the internally-powered, life-taxing, body-breaking Qiao numina of the Shih.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T08:58:08-07:00","id":593867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=593792#post593792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with a special k.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pentex's most popular cereal ^_^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These accusations are bullshit. You're going way off the track of what was actually in the books. Shih are gritty, scarred martial artist knights-errant that have a very small bag of tricks not even even close to Street Fighter (no wave-motion fists, no dragon punches, nothing of the sort). Strike Force Zero had personnel with a limited number of advanced prosthetics. So, yeah. Given the atmosphere presented in DHX (you're a scarred lone demon hunter who's kind of falling apart or a justifiably paranoid and scared secret agent with a few odd medical implants that only sort of mollify the tremendous gulf between you and the monsters), it's really not too out of place. </div> </div> </div>I often compared SF0 Agents to Hunters in terms of power level. Really enjoyed theirs and the Shih's back-story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=593703#post593703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">GDemon: The Fallen (It's as offensive from a religious perspective as Gypsies and KOTE is from a racial and cultural one)</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't really take that objection seriously. To do so would be to just take some extraordinary works of fiction and throw them out the door right along with Demon for some need to hold religion sacrosanct. Paradise Lost and Dante's Inferno both become utterly offensive. As to TV shows like Constantine and Supernatural, or movies following similar angles. Kevin Smith's Dogma gets thrown on the trash heap to.<br /> <br /> As would Werewolf! Because that's at least partly inspired by actual Native American religious practices, and so would be no less offensive than Demon. Denouncing people's right to express themselves creatively with religious ideas, and holding them somehow independent and sacrosanct as compared to other sorts of ideas, is inappropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T11:00:08-07:00","id":593993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=593703#post593703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gypsies is obviously number one for me for obvious reasons<br /> <br /> Other picks for me as well as my reasons for selecting them include...<br /> <br /> Kindred of the East (While not as racist as Gypsies, it comes in pretty damn close for me)<br /> <br /> Demon: The Fallen (It's as offensive from a religious perspective as Gypsies and KOTE is from a racial and cultural one)<br /> <br /> Time of Thin Blood (I don't like metaplot, so it ranks low for me. Plus if memory serves me correct, this is when they kill off the Ravnos, which sucks because I like them a lot. Dark Ages and early Revised really redeemed that clan/ And even 2e Ravnos are nowhere near as offensive as the very concept of Kuei-Jin in my opinion)<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia Tribebook Revised (Well, any of the Revised Clanbooks and Tribebooks rank low for me, due to the aforementioned metaplot. This one just stands out more and sucks for other non-metaplot reasons)<br /> <br /> Any of the Time of Judgment books (Gehenna, etc. Not really a fan of torching your own setting, though the metaplot and some poor choices in the initial game designs in 1e are to blame for these books. That and it was the 90s, so pre-millennial apocalyptic stuff was quite trendy then )<br /> <br /> New York By Night (Too railroady and metaplot-heavy in my opinion)<br /> <br /> Berlin By Night (Two words. Heinrich Himmler. That is all)<br /> <br /> Clanbook: Baali (Ewww.....)<br /> <br /> Charnel Houses of Europe: The Shoah (I understand that White Wolf did their best to be respectful to the subject material, and while it does retcon Berlin by Night, there are still certain subjects that RPG publishers, especially ones with the mixed history White Wolf in the 90's had, should not touch with a ten-foot pole. The Holocaust is one of these subjects. I'm sure the book itself is probably good from what I have heard, but the idea of it makes me very uncomfortable)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, I am actually kind of fine with Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand. It's not great, but it's not THAT bad either. At this point, I think it's so widely hated these days is because it's trendy to hate it. I mean, as weird as Soul Eaters are, it's a hell of a lot better than Gypsies, Demon: The Fallen, Vampire Nazis, or torching your own setting and then running like hell. Compared to the books I just mentioned, Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand is more &quot;meh&quot; than outright bad, at least to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gypsy yes of course. KotE *shrugs* I have less objection on the sense that KotE is bad for the reason a huge swath of CWoD was bad. Demon isn't even close to being on a worst of list. Demon's biggest offense was in the Earthbound book's section on Lucifer and real world religions. Beyond that I couldn't see it on any such list. Also &quot;has metaplot.&quot; is a really poor excuse to be a worst of list. Likewise Charnel Houses Europe was and is lauded as one of the more fantastic books that took strong subject matter seriously. I'll take those high praises over, &quot;It makes me uncomfortable.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T11:03:22-07:00","id":594009,"title":"","content":"As someone who lost family members and has studied the Holocaust I found that the Shoah book was respectful, not for everyone, and thought provoking. <br /> <br /> Demon Hunter X I found worked well with other Hunter types acolytes or kinfolk. While I feel the Stike Force 0 augmented humans with nifty bionic implants is more in line with Trinity or Aberrant I still prefer the book to the Revised Children of Gaia tribe book. <br /> <br /> Blood Dimmed Tides I like. I get warm tingling feelings as I plot a Technocracy story aboard the doomed station on the edge of the Marianas(sp) trench.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T11:05:52-07:00","id":594011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=593993#post593993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gypsy yes of course. KotE *shrugs* I have less objection on the sense that KotE is bad for the reason a huge swath of CWoD was bad. Demon isn't even close to being on a worst of list. Demon's biggest offense was in the Earthbound book's section on Lucifer and real world religions. Beyond that I couldn't see it on any such list. Also &quot;has metaplot.&quot; is a really poor excuse to be a worst of list. Likewise Charnel Houses Europe was and is lauded as one of the more fantastic books that took strong subject matter seriously. I'll take those high praises over, &quot;It makes me uncomfortable.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Same reason I wouldn't put Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand on the list. A lot of people hate it, but some got use out of it. Anyone who even tries to uses WOD:Gypsy is suspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T11:20:29-07:00","id":594022,"title":"","content":"I can understand someone thinking Demon as personaly offensive. If you hold to such beliefs as to think playing with demons unacceptable, and demons themselfs both irredeemable and that no fictional character should have opinions against your faith, so go ahead.<br /> <br /> As far as I know, Demon touched this subject closer, but never too close, to begin with. God is unknowable. Demons are a bunch with literally tainted perception. That aside, they had their reasons, but NEVER could really say what was going on on the other side. So you can still hold to almost any belief in the game. As I said, God, and His angels, are unknowable.<br /> <br /> By the way, a lot of people believe in a lot of things, and Demon never assumed a specific christian belief. The Torah never talk about &quot;The Enemy&quot;, and for some jewish theological scholars the Morningstar is still the highest of angels, his temptations against mankind being purely to test the people of God for Him. During the Middle Ages there where a lot of theological debates inside the Catholic Church, including the question about the possibility for a demon redeem himself, and a lot of people believed it could and, in some cases, would happen. Some interpretations of the Keys of Solomon go as far as to say some of the entities the work should be able to summon where redeemed by King Solomon in the face of God. By the way, the Keys of Solomon purpose to summon and bind demons for service to the faithful. In Islam, the Enemy of Mankind is Iblis, or Shaitan, and is a single entity that defied God only once, refusing to bow before the first humans, as God commanded the angels to do. Iblis takes the charge of tempting humans to sin to prove they're inferior to him, but is otherwise a faithful servant of God, enough to, even if exiled from Heaven, have the mercy to not go to Hell eiher, at least until the time of judgement, a mercy that human sinners don't have access to.<br /> <br /> So, all of this are actual beliefs. And there are even more among faithful believers. Not to talk about gnostics, mormons, kardecists, and, of course, the numerous non-christian people across the globe. There are also numerous works in the subject, in arts, philosophy, theology, politics and literature. Heck, even WoD itself! Vampire is 100% about religion, it touches the matter all the time. All WoD gamelines are, even if you're so blind as to not see it. Xamanistic animism, gnosticism, hinduism, buddism... the Thuatta de Danna, core to Changelings history is a pantheon from native religions in Ireland. Garou (with a lot of native american stuff, sure, but also beliefes from all across europe, the very word Garou coming from french) live, fight and die for religious beliefs all the fricking time. Whraith touches one of the most delicate of religious matter, the destiny of the soul. Mummy is based on one of the oldest and most respected, even if today not so followed, religious systems in human history. And you say DEMON CAN'T DO THIS!?<br /> <br /> Putting all that aside, you can say its offensive. BAD!? I can't agree, just can't. It is well writen, well tought, and gives a feeling at the same time new but not dissonant with the WoD in general.<br /> <br /> You can think Kung-Fu-East is good (and I'm not saying in my rantings its bad, or not gritty. I just don't see hem adding to the WoD), but Demon that bad? Seriously? For religious reasons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T11:32:48-07:00","id":594026,"title":"","content":"The reason why I personally find Demon: The Fallen offensive is because it outright states that all religions other than Christianity are evil religions created by the Earthbound. This includes my religion as well. And then it manages to potentially piss off Christians by saying that Satan created Christianity.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind that Demon was meant to be the very definite canon explanation to everything in the World of Darkness when it came out. Playing demons isn't the problem for me, it's the attacking of other people's religions by claiming every single religion but one are evil faiths created by eldritch abominations. And then insulting the one religion you don't directly disparage by stating that Lucifer, the being who is for lack of a better word, the main antagonist of said religion, invents it.<br /> <br /> Now can you see why I am offended by it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 07-17-2015, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T12:05:32-07:00","id":594036,"title":"","content":"I'd nominate <i>Midnight Circus</i> because it took a concept from a beloved Ray Bradbury novel and crapped all over it with hamfisted crudity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T12:48:19-07:00","id":594061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=594026#post594026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason why I personally find Demon: The Fallen offensive is because it outright states that all religions other than Christianity are evil religions created by the Earthbound. This includes my religion as well. And then it manages to potentially piss off Christians by saying that Satan created Christianity.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind that Demon was meant to be the very definite canon explanation to everything in the World of Darkness when it came out. Playing demons isn't the problem for me, it's the attacking of other people's religions by claiming every single religion but one are evil faiths created by eldritch abominations. And then insulting the one religion you don't directly disparage by stating that Lucifer, the being who is for lack of a better word, the main antagonist of said religion, invents it.<br /> <br /> Now can you see why I am offended by it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it said that about mine, too, mind you. Have I said at any point that I was christian, or even abrahamic, or atheist?<br /> <br /> Also, it isn't a definite canon explanation of anything, tough I also use as such a lot. Demons, agains, don't have all the answers, nor can be entirely thrust on averything they remember. As all the other splats, you can't take the line's books at face value.<br /> <br /> Since I didn't offended myself with Vampire stating that the original killer existed and God cursed all humankind with vampirism and Gehenna for it, and with Werewolf stating that my gods are just lesser spirits in the service of a Triatic Mad House, I see no reason for offend myself with Demon, even if sometimes I do find of poor taste to call my religion Earthbound nonsensical idolatry.<br /> <br /> Have I already said WW is full of traditional american prejudice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T13:17:22-07:00","id":594108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=594009#post594009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood Dimmed Tides I like. I get warm tingling feelings as I plot a Technocracy story aboard the doomed station on the edge of the Marianas(sp) trench.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know WHY I remembered it poorly... I must have had it confused with another book. I just reread the whole thing after getting into this discussion and realized &quot;nope, no this book is fantastic.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=594022#post594022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, Demon touched this subject closer, but never too close, to begin with. God is unknowable. Demons are a bunch with literally tainted perception. That aside, they had their reasons, but NEVER could really say what was going on on the other side. So you can still hold to almost any belief in the game. As I said, God, and His angels, are unknowable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I enjoyed the parallels with <i>Paradise Lost</i>, actually. The effort to portray Lucifer as a sympathetic character or tragic hero rather than bad man who did bad things for bad reasons, really stood out for me in both the epic poem and <i>Demon: The Fallen. </i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Putting all that aside, you can say its offensive. BAD!? I can't agree, just can't. It is well writen, well tought, and gives a feeling at the same time new but not dissonant with the WoD in general. </div> </div> </div>I love when White Wolf tries to tangle with the big philosophical questions! Were the Fallen wrong to turn against Heaven, even though they believed they were acting to save lives? Was their oath of obedience more morally obligatory than their need to behave compassionately? Do you listen to your conscience or to authority? And, if you've made a mistake can you ever really make up for it? They're an exquisite tragic hero, continuing the gothic tradition in the best possible way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=594026#post594026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason why I personally find Demon: The Fallen offensive is because it outright states that all religions other than Christianity are evil religions created by the Earthbound. This includes my religion as well. And then it manages to potentially piss off Christians by saying that Satan created Christianity.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, the World of Darkness isn't real. No statements made by characters in a game have any significance to your faith, which is related to the real world. Coincidentally, there are people in the real world who say your faith is bogus. I'd be more offended by them.<br /> <br /> Second, no it doesn't say that all other religions are created by Earthbound. This is patently false. It does say they maintain cults throughout the ages, but that's not the same thing. And the Earthbound didn't create the Garou faith, or the Catholic church (which also exists in WoD). So this statement is demonstrably false.<br /> <br /> Even if it were true, fictional Christianity in a fictional game is not your religion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bear in mind that Demon was meant to be the very definite canon explanation to everything in the World of Darkness when it came out. Playing demons isn't the problem for me, it's the attacking of other people's religions by claiming every single religion but one are evil faiths created by eldritch abominations. And then insulting the one religion you don't directly disparage by stating that Lucifer, the being who is for lack of a better word, the main antagonist of said religion, invents it. </div> </div> </div>Actually? No it wasn't. White Wolf has explicitly stated that none of the cosmologies is necessarily &quot;more right&quot; than any of the others, not even Demon's. They stated that because approving one over the other would would potentially undercut the narrative value of the other franchises. They spent an eternity in a pit of madness, and had their memories colored by spite, while now trying to recall the full breadth of Angelic memories through the miniscule space of a human brain. It's very unlikely their recollections are totally correct, or possibly not even partially correct.<br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness, no one is right. Or more accurately, everyone is wrong. One of the most interesting possible solutions is that ALL of the cosmologies are true all at once, because creation occurred at a time with little or no banality when both time and causality had different meanings than we understand now as we exist in the corrupted and dying world on the verge of apocalypse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now can you see why I am offended by it? </div> </div> </div>An imaginary world, set in the worst possible reality where everything is wrong and even the creator is capricious, leaving you abandoned in darkness managed to cross the fourth wall to offend your faith.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is meant to be a hopeless reality, that means nothing is pure and there are no true good guys. That's the whole idea. It's fantasy.<br /> <br /> In that context? No, I cannot see why you are offended.<br /> <br /> In any table top game, it's very important to understand the difference between players and characters. Between story and reality. And to ensure that characters (not players) are offended. It's just a game, and in it we've posed a hypothetical worst-case universe to explore. You can't do that without upsetting religious ideologies. They give hope. Hope must give way in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T13:50:02-07:00","id":594124,"title":"","content":"I consider me self an atheist. I do not believe in higher powers. Therefore in some way all WoD book is offensive to my believe system.<br /> Believe in science and human genius is mocked be existence of supernatural creature and god like entities.<br /> Even science is only a form of magick created by consensus.<br /> <br /> In Word of Darkness people like me are blind fools used like sustenance or pawns in hand of greater powers. <br /> But that is not reason for be offended.<br /> <br /> I do not think White Wolf or Onyx do this in purpose to offend somebody and like DarkExcalibur42 says it is only imaginary world, set in the worst possible reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5536-arkilijo","name":"Arkilijo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T14:28:59-07:00","id":594140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=594026#post594026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason why I personally find Demon: The Fallen offensive is because it outright states that all religions other than Christianity are evil religions created by the Earthbound. This includes my religion as well. And then it manages to potentially piss off Christians by saying that Satan created Christianity.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind that Demon was meant to be the very definite canon explanation to everything in the World of Darkness when it came out. Playing demons isn't the problem for me, it's the attacking of other people's religions by claiming every single religion but one are evil faiths created by eldritch abominations. And then insulting the one religion you don't directly disparage by stating that Lucifer, the being who is for lack of a better word, the main antagonist of said religion, invents it.<br /> <br /> Now can you see why I am offended by it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember when Demon came out (Demon and Mage were the ones I followed religiously back then, no pun intended.) I think a lot of fans did try to use Demon's cosmology explanation as a &quot;definite canon&quot; because of the multiple layers of reality approach that could let someone rationalize the Werewolf triad, a Vampire/Demon Biblical backstory, and pretty much any other culture's religious creation story as alternate layers. Basically &quot;all are true, from a certain point of view.&quot; But IIRC, there was never anything official about Demon being &quot;canon&quot; across the globe. Demon's backstory is canon for Demon, just like Werewolf's is canon for Werewolf, Vampire's for Vampire and so on. Demon's just had more attention at the time because it, and Mummy, were the last ones published.<br /> <br /> Please don't think I'm trying to say you're wrong to be offended though. I love the game, but it is really not for everyone and I wouldn't blame anyone for being offended on religious grounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T14:40:28-07:00","id":594152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=594026#post594026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason why I personally find Demon: The Fallen offensive is because it outright states that all religions other than Christianity are evil religions created by the Earthbound. This includes my religion as well. And then it manages to potentially piss off Christians by saying that Satan created Christianity.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind that Demon was meant to be the very definite canon explanation to everything in the World of Darkness when it came out. Playing demons isn't the problem for me, it's the attacking of other people's religions by claiming every single religion but one are evil faiths created by eldritch abominations. And then insulting the one religion you don't directly disparage by stating that Lucifer, the being who is for lack of a better word, the main antagonist of said religion, invents it.<br /> <br /> Now can you see why I am offended by it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I specifically mentioned that part of Earthbound. Though the latter part really doesn't bother me. The &quot;pagan religions are EVUL.&quot; was distasteful because it was hamfisted. The latter at least has nuance for what is a piece of fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T15:20:58-07:00","id":594187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkilijo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=594124#post594124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I consider me self an atheist. I do not believe in higher powers. Therefore in some way all WoD book is offensive to my believe system.<br /> Believe in science and human genius is mocked be existence of supernatural creature and god like entities.<br /> Even science is only a form of magick created by consensus.<br /> <br /> In Word of Darkness people like me are blind fools used like sustenance or pawns in hand of greater powers.<br /> But that is not reason for be offended.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should write that down and use it as the driving personality behind a Hunter Zealot. The existence of the supernatural is a mockery of humanity and must by wholly purged so that we might exist free from their metaphysical tyranny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T15:29:02-07:00","id":594195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkExcalibur42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=594187#post594187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You should write that down and use it as the driving personality behind a Hunter Zealot. The existence of the supernatural is a mockery of humanity and must by wholly purged so that we might exist free from their metaphysical tyranny.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's way more Vision than Zeal, because it's the Wayward credo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T23:43:39-07:00","id":594524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I specifically mentioned that part of Earthbound. Though the latter part really doesn't bother me. The &quot;pagan religions are EVUL.&quot; was distasteful because it was hamfisted. The latter at least has nuance for what is a piece of fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I think that too. Also, it's just wrong in a crossover with Mage (you're basically stating that many of your main characters likely worship some evil demon). It leaves you with few choice but to state that said part it's just Earthbound paranoia (they see enemy demons everywhere), and that they don't have as much power over religions as they believe.<br /> <br /> Appart from that, I loved that book. The Lovecraftian feeling it's very good (perhaps the most Lovecraftian book in cWoD).<br /> <br /> I don't like the Changeling Nunnehi (I think they're in the player's guide, but I don't remember), a bunch of stereotypical indians that have little to do with the spirit of Changeling, if you ask me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkExcalibur42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, the World of Darkness isn't real. No statements made by characters in a game have any significance to your faith, which is related to the real world. Coincidentally, there are people in the real world who say your faith is bogus. I'd be more offended by them.<br /> ...<br /> fictional Christianity in a fictional game is not your religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that this same argument can be used to justify Gypsies: &quot;Hey, they're not real world Gypsies, it's just an innocent work of fiction&quot;.<br /> I find weird that mocking ethnic groups it's wrong, but mocking religions it's perfectly ok, and should be defended. Can someone explain this to me?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T23:56:34-07:00","id":594527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=594524#post594524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that this same argument can be used to justify Gypsies: &quot;Hey, they're not real world Gypsies, it's just an innocent work of fiction&quot;.<br /> I find weird that mocking ethnic groups it's wrong, but mocking religions it's perfectly ok, and should be defended. Can someone explain this to me?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that there's a difference in the sense that Christianity is still basically the most powerful religion in the world. So when you mock Christianity, you're essentially mocking a religion that is either your own religion or one that is generally more dominant and occasionally more oppressive than your own. You're &quot;punching upward&quot; so to speak. While Christianity is often caricaturized, they're generally too dominant to be truly harmed by it. (Though, it's my understanding that many of the critics of Demon the Fallen are members of non-Christian religions, so in their case, it wouldn't be a &quot;punching upward&quot; situation.)<br /> <br /> The Roma however are not a dominant racial group. They still face a lot of discrimination and caricatures have been used as justification for a lot of mistreatment by more dominant ethnic groups. So by mocking Roma, you're &quot;punching downward&quot; in a way that could legitimately hurt a group of people.<br /> <br /> I've never actually heard of the Nunnehi. Can you elaborate on how they don't fit in with Changeling? (I've always liked the idea of Changeling, but I don't actually know much about it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 07-18-2015, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T01:23:17-07:00","id":594585,"title":"","content":"But what about mocking the other religions?. Christians haven't been mocked that much. While the devil defended christianity, it's also hinted that Christ might have been an incarnation of the True, with capital T, God. In contrast, minor religions like pagan faiths and hinduism where much more insulted (they adore Cthulhu. Well, I have to admit that mocking politheism in that way it's downright Lovecraftian by itself).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've never actually heard of the Nunnehi. Can you elaborate on how they don't fit in with Changeling? (I've always liked the idea of Changeling, but I don't actually know much about it.) </div> </div> </div>As far as I know:<br /> <br /> The Nunnehi are the &quot;native american&quot; dreams. They're Changeling, usually (but not always) depicted as the stereotypical &quot;noble salvaje&quot; or &quot;spiritual indian&quot;.<br /> <br /> They can't pursue &quot;modern dreams&quot; like normal Changelings to get Glamour from creativity, love, etc... they can only gain Glamour from artworks that are &quot;native&quot;, that it's, traditional native american artworks, as appropriate to their trib...er...culture. Or, alternatively, they can recharge in Caer...erm...in natural places untouched by the white man<br /> <br /> They don't enter in the Dreaming (albeit they did, in the past), instead they enter in the Umbra.<br /> <br /> And, of course, they are enemy of the european Changeling, because they invaded their lands. How could be otherwise?<br /> <br /> Basically, they're the Uktena/Wendigo version of faeries. Just more stereotypical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T02:12:41-07:00","id":594595,"title":"","content":"I'm willing to cut White Wolf some slack for their really early stuff. yes, Berlin by Night was godawful, but really the game was only <i>just</i> out of its &quot;xerox copies held together with paper clips&quot; phase, so we can't really demand perfection. or all that much quality from this period.<br /> <br /> Most of the usual suspects have been cited. Gypsies, Tribebook: CoG, Bloo-Dimmed Tides, etc. So I'm just going to avoid the &quot;garbage&quot; period of Vampire, and the social commentary stuff, and get right into the meat of <i>bad books</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Bastet</b> was terrible. Okay, fine, your first shot at a breedbook, it's not going ot be stunning. But it's painfully clear Phil Brucato would have rather been writing a Mage supplement instead of this. In fact it reads like he was trying to turn it into one. And of course we a;; expect every splatbook to basically go &quot;we're the best, everyone else sucks,&quot; but the bastet book just goes WAAAAAY overboard on the Mary Sue-ness. It creates a whole lot of jargon which exists solely to create the illusion that Bastet are <i>like totally different</i> - but they're really not, they're just more Jargon-y. Which is another problem. The Breed book didn't really make any efforts to make them more than &quot;Garou who doink big cats.&quot; Most (not all) of the Breed Books create a fairly compelling new outlook unique to that breed, but the bastet are just like &quot;pffft, Wyrm, Weaver and Wyld? That's dog nonsense! Come listen about Cahlash, Rajah, and Nala, the TRUTH!&quot; - hurk, huuuurk! The artwork was uniformly terrible (save for <i>most</i> of the Ron Spencer - even he has some bad ones in this) and the design is not great.<br /> <br /> <b>Nuwisha:</b> if Bastet was too much fluff for too little interesting stuff, Nuwisha was the opposite. it's a book for an entire changing breed, and it's like ten pages smaller than any of the 2nd edition tribe books! I actually bought this one off the shelf for $12 - fifty cents a page, almost! They get Garou breed and Ragabash Gifts, then their own list... The Nuwisha came off less like an independent breed, and more like &quot;The skinny Ragabash tribe.&quot; They could have gone places and instead we get half the information we need (what are the special maneuvers those totems give? What's the Nuwisha starting Willpower? What are these Gifts and rites that you are making errata for, they're not in this book!) and only a quarter of the information we <i>want</i>. The art is pretty generic middle-period WoD, and is frequently cartoony - which doesn't help the &quot;goofball syndrome&quot; this book alternately discourages and encourages.<br /> <br /> <b>Havens of the damned</b> simply did not need to exist. MTV Cribz for vampires. <i>MAYBE</i> if there had been more to it? Throw a module in the back. Put in some splat-by-splat general info beyond the <i>specific havens</i>. Outlines for how domain is handled in different situations, etc. It was never going to be a <i>great</i> book, but it could have been more than it was.<br /> <br /> <b>War in Concordia</b> is another &quot;didn't need to exist&quot; book. Changeling had so much <i>basic stuff</i> left undone. At least a REAL Boggan kithbook, guys! A 2nd edition player's guide wouldn't have killed anyone, honest! But no, we get this tome about how to set fire to your changeling game because White Wolf wasn't going to support it anymore.<br /> <br /> <b>Destiny's Price</b> is, hands-down, the goofiest, most inept book I've ever read. I'm sorry to the author but there is no more surefire way to sweep me up into a fit of giggles than someone writing about &quot;da skreetz, yo&quot; than when they are doing so in a microsoft word document in an air-conditioned office, to create a book for a game about Harry Potter vs. Agent Smith (I know mage is &quot;more than that&quot; so spare me, folks.) It is the HEIGHT of pretension, in a game line already famed for its pretension, from a company known for pretense. it is staggeringly bad and ludicrous. The specific iformation isn't <i>bad</i> game-wise, but the delivery and presentation is just mind-bogglingly lame (or as <i>Destiny's Price</i> itself would say, &quot;Yo G homie-dawgs, dis here 'zine be trey whack yo dig for shizzle, no beef whuddup! Pssst shit fuck fuck shit hookers, wuuuuuuurd&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T02:37:22-07:00","id":594598,"title":"","content":"Can I nominated <b>Blood Treachery</b> and <b>the Red Sign</b>?<br /> <br /> For me, both seemed to come off as 'You want a crossover book? Fine, we'll give you two, and show you just how much crossovers suck!'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T04:49:20-07:00","id":594637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=594527#post594527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that there's a difference in the sense that Christianity is still basically the most powerful religion in the world. So when you mock Christianity, you're essentially mocking a religion that is either your own religion or one that is generally more dominant and occasionally more oppressive than your own. You're &quot;punching upward&quot; so to speak. While Christianity is often caricaturized, they're generally too dominant to be truly harmed by it. (Though, it's my understanding that many of the critics of Demon the Fallen are members of non-Christian religions, so in their case, it wouldn't be a &quot;punching upward&quot; situation.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully endorse the mocking Christianity, Islam, Satanism, Agnosticism, Atheism, and any other thing that comes to mind. Any and every ideology ought to be mocked, including this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=594524#post594524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that this same argument can be used to justify Gypsies: &quot;Hey, they're not real world Gypsies, it's just an innocent work of fiction&quot;.<br /> I find weird that mocking ethnic groups it's wrong, but mocking religions it's perfectly ok, and should be defended. Can someone explain this to me?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Roma however are not a dominant racial group. They still face a lot of discrimination and caricatures have been used as justification for a lot of mistreatment by more dominant ethnic groups. So by mocking Roma, you're &quot;punching downward&quot; in a way that could legitimately hurt a group of people.<br /> <br /> I've never actually heard of the Nunnehi. Can you elaborate on how they don't fit in with Changeling? (I've always liked the idea of Changeling, but I don't actually know much about it.) </div> </div> </div>They're people. That's the difference. Mocking philosophies and ideologies is perfectly fine. Caricaturing an entire race of people is not cool. This can get fuzzy at times because of how much overlap there often is between the perception of a people and their ideas (which include faiths). If I published a WoD book that talked about how all the Italians were greasy crime bosses, that would be wrong. If I published a book that made fun of organized crime, saying &quot;hey it turns out they're actually all unwitting dupes working for a Demon and bringing about the apocalypse&quot; that's fine. If I published a book that portrayed all Christian characters as religious zealots who go off on killing sprees, that's wrong. If I publish a book that says &quot;hey, all those Christians? They don't know it... but they're following a sham,&quot; that's fine. There's a difference between racial stereotyping and and hypothetically questioning a system of thought, faith, ideology, gov't, etc. One is about people. The other is about things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=594585#post594585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what about mocking the other religions?. Christians haven't been mocked that much. While the devil defended christianity, it's also hinted that Christ might have been an incarnation of the True, with capital T, God. In contrast, minor religions like pagan faiths and hinduism where much more insulted (they adore Cthulhu. Well, I have to admit that mocking politheism in that way it's downright Lovecraftian by itself).</div> </div> </div> </div>Religions are ideas. All ideas should be mocked. Those which can survive this baptism, which is a continual process, are worth keeping.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ... the stereotypical &quot;noble salvaje&quot; or &quot;spiritual indian&quot;. </div> </div> </div>This is what's wrong with it. Stereotyping groups of people is bad. ._. It stagnates thinking, stops questions. Posing the hypothetical that a faith is false, stimulates thinking. Promotes questions.<br /> <br /> Critical thinking above all else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6883,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","user":"DarkExcalibur42","date":". 07-18-2015, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T09:49:44-07:00","id":594816,"title":"","content":"I've been rethinking this some. I think there is a difference in terms of religion and race in terms of a game line, because often in a game line, the storyteller has to decide what creation story is true for their game. Demon the Fallen is a bit more explicit about it, but really, any Vampire game that actually features Caine has made the same choice in terms of what is true for the particular story. Essentially, one religion (or no religion) will be &quot;right&quot; in terms of a game, the others are misguided somehow.<br /> <br /> That said, given all of the negative experiences people have had regarding religious oppression and persecution, it's perfectly understandable that many folk will be upset or offended by the treatment of their religion. In the real world, it's not really enough to just say &quot;we're only mocking an idea&quot; when people have been tortured and killed based on those ideas. Demon is a great game, but it's a game that is based around Christian ideas (whether it upholds or deconstructs them) and not everyone is going to be okay with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T10:40:47-07:00","id":594839,"title":"","content":"Not being okay is valid, saying is bad because of that is goofish.<br /> <br /> Again, I AM one of the mocked there! But its about belief, about an idea. The game said I'm wrong in my belief. It didn't said I was a savage or a killer or anything, just that one idea I can't proove is, in setting, prooven wrong (and, as already discussed, not even this is entirely true).<br /> <br /> But when the book says that all south-american countries are so poor that there are only one car per comunity and people die regularly of sepsis and malarya, when they insist on using &quot;third world&quot; to describe countries they don't have the slytest idea of how they really are aside american prejudice, then they're talking about my people. And about how we live. THEN its outright ofensive. It depicts me and my family as savages without education and on a lower cultural level.<br /> <br /> That's a LOT of differences between Demon and Gypsies in that regard...<br /> <br /> Nunnehi are a good example, indeed. One separate class of Dreams just for native americans, full of &quot;indian feel&quot; but no &quot;human feel&quot; whatsoever, as if only the european where capable of dream the full spectrum of the Dreaming, and these noble savages where dreaming just with rivers and trees.<br /> <br /> Kung-Fu-East have a lot of it, also, tough not so much. They surely read a lot about Taoism, Confucionism and Chinese Mythology. But there ARE a lot more to Asia than that. Most of Russia, to begin with, a nation with literaly hundreds of ethnic groups. And to the south, the complexity of history on India, China, Korea, Japan, just to exemplify a few COMPLETELY DISTINCT countries, each with LOTS of distinct ethnic groups, cultures, mindsets. India alone is maybe as diverse as the entire european continent. But for WoD is just Ravnos' county, because Gypsy Ravnos was ill received...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T12:49:23-07:00","id":594917,"title":"","content":"Alright, on the subject of Demon, I guess I did kind of overreact. It is just a work of fiction at the end of the day and White Wolf didn't mean any harm by their writings. Either way, I apologize for my overreaction earlier and I will quietly bow out of this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T16:56:04-07:00","id":595118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=594598#post594598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I nominated <b>Blood Treachery</b> and <b>the Red Sign</b>?<br /> <br /> For me, both seemed to come off as 'You want a crossover book? Fine, we'll give you two, and show you just how much crossovers suck!'</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, don't get me started on the idiocy of <i>The Red Sign</i>. While I think the basic premise was interesting enough, at least half of the text in that book was devoted to bloviation about how groundbreaking and special the next part was going to be... any minute now... just you wait and see... no really, we're serious... it's going to knock your players' socks off. And I'm sorry, but why include obvious pastiche/knockoffs of the <i>Necronomicon</i> and <i>The King in Yellow</i> that don't actually do the things those accursed works are supposed to? Lovecraft and Chambers are both in the public domain; go hog wild and feature a book that can open the gateway for the Old Ones or a play that can make readers victims of its fictional supernatural namesake after it's driven them crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T17:38:37-07:00","id":595169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=594816#post594816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been rethinking this some. I think there is a difference in terms of religion and race in terms of a game line, because often in a game line, the storyteller has to decide what creation story is true for their game. Demon the Fallen is a bit more explicit about it, but really, any Vampire game that actually features Caine has made the same choice in terms of what is true for the particular story. Essentially, one religion (or no religion) will be &quot;right&quot; in terms of a game, the others are misguided somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The WoD is a strange, contradictory one. Many things can be true together, even if they would exclude each other. All of their creation stories could be true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T22:17:01-07:00","id":595388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkExcalibur42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're people. That's the difference. Mocking philosophies and ideologies is perfectly fine. Caricaturing an entire race of people is not cool. This can get fuzzy at times because of how much overlap there often is between the perception of a people and their ideas (which include faiths). If I published a WoD book that talked about how all the Italians were greasy crime bosses, that would be wrong. If I published a book that made fun of organized crime, saying &quot;hey it turns out they're actually all unwitting dupes working for a Demon and bringing about the apocalypse&quot; that's fine. If I published a book that portrayed all Christian characters as religious zealots who go off on killing sprees, that's wrong. If I publish a book that says &quot;hey, all those Christians? They don't know it... but they're following a sham,&quot; that's fine. There's a difference between racial stereotyping and and hypothetically questioning a system of thought, faith, ideology, gov't, etc. One is about people. The other is about things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well put. I note that, while Demon mocks (to some extent), it doesn't stereotype. And that's a world of difference.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T23:31:07-07:00","id":595410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=593623#post593623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the East As Kung Fu material? First, it did an entire hemisphere, and in fact the one with MOST people, just be barred to anything stablished by the other lines. Caine was one of the first humans and the first vampires, e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except if you, you know... follow Werewolf or Mage and then he's 100 thousand years or so too late. Hell the Ravnos Antedeluvian if he's Ravana predates the creation of the world by 2 million years with the &quot;caine myth&quot;.Or to continue the &quot;Caine myth is silly&quot; with biblical literalism put it in this perspective <a href=\"http://www.theonion.com/article/sumerians-look-on-in-confusion-as-god-creates-worl-2879\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.theonion.com/article/sume...ates-worl-2879</a><br /> <br /> D:TF creates whole tired setup to try and get around this but if you don't accept the &quot;demon is right&quot; then there's no reason Vampire should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T02:46:34-07:00","id":595507,"title":"","content":"Yes and no, because there are no dates, and I'm not saying Vampire's creation myth have to be taken at face value. In fact, Caine was just an example, and the whole thing is meaningless.<br /> <br /> What DOES have meaning is that in Vampire, Vampires are the most important creatures around. It doesn't have to be valid for the WoD as a whole, obviously, but it IS relevant for the line to not break this concept, since they're the protagonists, and it IS relevant to the WoD in general for them to be common and powerful enough for this assumption to at least make sense.<br /> <br /> In the end, the problem is that they declared an entire hemisphere almost devoid of the very creatures they started WoD with, around whom they made the Antediluvians, the beings that achieved command over the Abyss and parts of the Dark Umbra.<br /> <br /> Because those creatures where expelled by undead Kung-Fu masters that are their counterpart and better in every respect.<br /> <br /> As I said, I don't think the East material to be bad by itself. Its bad by context. Its f*cking stupid to outshine yourself making everything in the East being more awesome than the Western counterpart in a way that makes your own main setting seems just a lot of morons.<br /> <br /> Nothing against a setting MADE to support this view from the start, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T04:54:08-07:00","id":595542,"title":"","content":"You may be looking at it wrong and interpreting KotE as a Vampire supplement instead of it being a game of its own. As frankly the whole book beats you over the head with the fact that it doesn't give a fuck about Cainites. It's a book that has more commonalities with Wraith and Werewolf then it ever will with Vampire. And just like Werewolf laughs at anything Vampire has to say about how the universe works, so does KotE.<br /> <br /> And while I'd definitely pitch Children of Gaia Revised for one of the worst books I have ever endured, I'd like to stand up in defense of Blood Dimmed Tides and Shoah. One has an amazing ammount of hooks and ideas to be used, and the other shows an immense respect and tact in handling a difficult subject matter. That and Infernalism are few of the actually useful Black Dog Games.<br /> <br /> I noticed noone pitched WoD: Combat. That book was a horrid mess of poorly researched fight stuff with horribly bad overcomplicated mechanics. It's a testament to its badness that some people still think they should use rules from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 07-19-2015, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T06:29:22-07:00","id":595576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=595507#post595507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and no, because there are no dates, and I'm not saying Vampire's creation myth have to be taken at face value. In fact, Caine was just an example, and the whole thing is meaningless.</div> </div> </div> </div>No the caine thing does matter, because the East has been a source of &quot;maybe they are wrong about it&quot; since 1992. The &quot;vampires don't exist in Asia&quot; is as much a basis in the setting as &quot;Werewolves hate vampires&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What DOES have meaning is that in Vampire, Vampires are the most important creatures around. It doesn't have to be valid for the WoD as a whole, obviously, but it IS relevant for the line to not break this concept, since they're the protagonists, and it IS relevant to the WoD in general for them to be common and powerful enough for this assumption to at least make sense. </div> </div> </div><br /> No they don't. Compare the various incarnations of mummy. Do they have &quot;have to let vampires be super powerful&quot; in comparison? They tend to be handing vampires their asses all over the place. Because Mummies from the mummy book are the protagonists. Same with werewolves, mages etc. Or we can look at the various kindred sects Cam books treat the other factions as Jokes, the most recent anarch book does the same and so on and so forth. The thing presented for players is going to be the most important thing from the focus of that line period. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the end, the problem is that they declared an entire hemisphere almost devoid of the very creatures they started WoD with, around whom they made the Antediluvians, the beings that achieved command over the Abyss and parts of the Dark Umbra. </div> </div> </div>If we are going to references to End Times books Ascension says a single Archmaster is why Necromancy is &quot;icky&quot; in the world of Darkness including stuff like why the Giovanni are working on destroying the shroud. This isn't even him acting intentionally but just his Resonence acting on the universe. So no Antedeluvians aren't treated as super gods. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because those creatures where expelled by undead Kung-Fu masters that are their counterpart and better in every respect.<br /> <br /> As I said, I don't think the East material to be bad by itself. Its bad by context. Its f*cking stupid to outshine yourself making everything in the East being more awesome than the Western counterpart in a way that makes your own main setting seems just a lot of morons.<br /> <br /> Nothing against a setting MADE to support this view from the start, though. </div> </div> </div>It was. 1992 the first book to cover the world in general described nonkindred vampires as being the dominant power in Asia with afew places Kindred having made inroads. It predates werewolf and mage having theriown games. I cannot more think of &quot;from the start&quot; than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T07:47:08-07:00","id":595630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=595576#post595576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are going to references to End Times books Ascension says a single Archmaster is why Necromancy is &quot;icky&quot; in the world of Darkness including stuff like why the Giovanni are working on destroying the shroud. This isn't even him acting intentionally but just his Resonence acting on the universe. So no Antedeluvians aren't treated as super gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... Yeah, they still are treated as &quot;super gods&quot;. The Ravnos antideluvian required a spirit nuke at ground zero (after already fighting off three bodhisattvas for an indeterminate amount of time) to <i>weaken</i> him enough for focused orbital mirrors to finally finish him off. That's pretty damn &quot;super god&quot;. Just because the setting has other massively powerful beings doesn't mean the antediluvians aren't also massively powerful, nor does it imply the setting itself is calling them somehow lesser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T08:00:50-07:00","id":595642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=595542#post595542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may be looking at it wrong and interpreting KotE as a Vampire supplement instead of it being a game of its own. As frankly the whole book beats you over the head with the fact that it doesn't give a fuck about Cainites. It's a book that has more commonalities with Wraith and Werewolf then it ever will with Vampire. And just like Werewolf laughs at anything Vampire has to say about how the universe works, so does KotE.<br /> <br /> And while I'd definitely pitch Children of Gaia Revised for one of the worst books I have ever endured, I'd like to stand up in defense of Blood Dimmed Tides and Shoah. One has an amazing ammount of hooks and ideas to be used, and the other shows an immense respect and tact in handling a difficult subject matter. That and Infernalism are few of the actually useful Black Dog Games.<br /> <br /> I noticed noone pitched WoD: Combat. That book was a horrid mess of poorly researched fight stuff with horribly bad overcomplicated mechanics. It's a testament to its badness that some people still think they should use rules from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>[X-Men vs Street Fighter Announcer Voice] THIS IS WORLD OF DARKNESS VERSUS STREET FIGHTER! [/X-Men vs Street Fighter Announcer Voice]<br /> <br /> Don't you just love how learning to snap someone's neck requires more effort than it takes to get most supernatural powers? Wait, no, not love. Hate. Hate how you have to spend 20 xp after getting joint lock and joint break and Brawl 5 just to get a combat maneuver that should be really easy for supernaturally strong monsters to accomplish. Or how Dodge turned into the Block Technique from Street Fighter, and damage from your iron body training to others was based on how high your Dodge was.<br /> <br /> Also, the Skill you used for bows and thrown weapons was Melee, at least going by the sample characters. Also, Do picked up more lower-key super moves.<br /> <br /> You could go on and on about the missteps, there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T09:50:22-07:00","id":595739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=595630#post595630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err... Yeah, they still are treated as &quot;super gods&quot;. The Ravnos antideluvian required a spirit nuke at ground zero (after already fighting off three bodhisattvas for an indeterminate amount of time) to <i>weaken</i> him enough for focused orbital mirrors to finally finish him off. That's pretty damn &quot;super god&quot;. Just because the setting has other massively powerful beings doesn't mean the antediluvians aren't also massively powerful, nor does it imply the setting itself is calling them somehow lesser.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No he didn't. The 3 KJ would have killed him. But then some Garou got involved and attacked them. Then the Technocracy attacked everyone. Really its a clusterfuck. I am not saying the Antes aren't scary powerful, but they aren't the end all be all of power which is what I was getting at. There are many things more powerful than them that get taken out. Hell the conceit that they are ancient bloodgods compared to other kindred undercuts the war of ages, there should be a damned good reason they are playing hidden games rather than ruling as undisputed blood gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T11:05:57-07:00","id":595775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=595739#post595739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No he didn't. The 3 KJ would have killed him. But then some Garou got involved and attacked them. Then the Technocracy attacked everyone. Really its a clusterfuck.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Might </i>have killed him. I'm seeing absolutely no references to garou in Time of Thin Blood or Guide to the Technocracy involved in the fight, so I'm not sure where you got that from. What the books do say is the three <i>didn't</i> take down the Rav Ante after fighting day and night. Then a magic bomb got dropped on them all and disrupted the Bodhis' super-storm-weapons by killing everything <i>except</i> the ravnos Antediluvian. He died because the battle weakened him enough for the sunlight mirrors to finish the job. Even assuming there were garou present who only wanted to fight the Bodhisattvas for whatever reasons, it's clear who survived the what killed everything else, and who only died because the fight weakened him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=595739#post595739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell the conceit that they are ancient bloodgods compared to other kindred undercuts the war of ages, there should be a damned good reason they are playing hidden games rather than ruling as undisputed blood gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's already plenty of damn good reasons: each other, mortals bringing about Inquisition 2.0, Caine himself, torpor, and of course all the younglings rising up to hold Anarch Revolt Revised and do to them what was done to [Tzimisce] and [Lasombra] (supposedly, I know). You don't need to add fear of archmages and kuei-jin to the mix to make it plausible when they have plenty of plausible reasons for choosing a behind-the-scenes approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T11:33:40-07:00","id":595805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=595775#post595775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Might </i>have killed him. I'm seeing absolutely no references to garou in Time of Thin Blood or Guide to the Technocracy involved in the fight, so I'm not sure where you got that from. What the books do say is the three <i>didn't</i> take down the Rav Ante after fighting day and night. Then a magic bomb got dropped on them all and disrupted the Bodhis' super-storm-weapons by killing everything <i>except</i> the ravnos Antediluvian. He died because the battle weakened him enough for the sunlight mirrors to finish the job. Even assuming there were garou present who only wanted to fight the Bodhisattvas for whatever reasons, it's clear who survived the what killed everything else, and who only died because the fight weakened him.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were still going strong, though, and a prophecy related in the Nagah breed book and perhaps other places noted that two of the Boddhisattavas would have died, but they would have killed Zapathasura.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's already plenty of damn good reasons: each other, mortals bringing about Inquisition 2.0, Caine himself, torpor, and of course all the younglings rising up to hold Anarch Revolt Revised and do to them what was done to [Tzimisce] and [Lasombra] (supposedly, I know). You don't need to add fear of archmages and kuei-jin to the mix to make it plausible when they have plenty of plausible reasons for choosing a behind-the-scenes approach. </div> </div> </div>What do the third gens fear from any of those if they're literal blood gods? The power level that you posit makes just about all of it moot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T11:49:27-07:00","id":595824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=595542#post595542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I noticed noone pitched WoD: Combat. That book was a horrid mess of poorly researched fight stuff with horribly bad overcomplicated mechanics. It's a testament to its badness that some people still think they should use rules from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to pitch Combat for me, because I really enjoyed Street Fighter: the Storytelling Game (which it is a rehash of). I am immensely sad that they never got the chance to release a Darkstalkers book. (And if Capcom ever agreed to allow them to be released on Drive Thru, I'd have the set that day.)<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Combat tried to shoehorn it into WoD, and wound up breaking both in the attempt.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T12:09:58-07:00","id":595837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=595805#post595805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do the third gens fear from any of those if they're literal blood gods? The power level that you posit makes just about all of it moot.</div> </div> </div> </div>The level of power I'm positing acknowledges that antediluvians have, in the past, (maybe) died at the hands of the first anarch revolt (Lasombra Ante) and their own childer (Cappadocius, possibly Brujah) and dying is awful inconvenient. Caine, as their grand-daddy and prophesied to kill them in the end of days is certainly something you'd want to avoid noticing you as long as possible, and would have been someone most of them know is real, having met him. Torpor doesn't seem like something you can just out-power. I can only guess the issue you take with my statement is more with a hypothetical Inquisition 2.0, which granted doesn't seem likely to be an instant death sentence, but would surely not be a fun time to go through when you could <i>still exert your power from behind the scenes</i>.<br /> <br /> Of course, if there are mega-more-powerful Kuei-Jin wandering around, as you posit, your argument works against you: why aren't <i>they</i> the ones ruling as literal blood/chi gods?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T14:59:13-07:00","id":596119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=595824#post595824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's hard to pitch Combat for me, because I really enjoyed Street Fighter: the Storytelling Game (which it is a rehash of). I am immensely sad that they never got the chance to release a Darkstalkers book. (And if Capcom ever agreed to allow them to be released on Drive Thru, I'd have the set that day.)<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Combat tried to shoehorn it into WoD, and wound up breaking both in the attempt.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of a Street Fighter RPG, and some of the fluff (like the Shadoloo stuff) was amazing. But the rules were... meh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T15:01:13-07:00","id":596120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=595837#post595837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, if there are mega-more-powerful Kuei-Jin wandering around, as you posit, your argument works against you: why aren't <i>they</i> the ones ruling as literal blood/chi gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they are way beyond such paltry concerns as being Gods among men. They are the enlightened beings whose actual existence and power is predicated on being beyond trivial matters and embracing some pretty damn odd values. They are there to help others along the path, not indulge in petty temporal things.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T15:15:32-07:00","id":596152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=596120#post596120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because they are way beyond such paltry concerns as being Gods among men. They are the enlightened beings whose actual existence and power is predicated on being beyond trivial matters and embracing some pretty damn odd values. They are there to help others along the path, not indulge in petty temporal things.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I tought about answering each statement, but you summed it all yourself here.<br /> <br /> That's PRECISELY what I find bad abou KotE. REALLY bad.<br /> <br /> As I said twice or trice before, nothing against it as a setting by itself. But in WoD?<br /> <br /> You like KotE? Great. You probably plays it differently than you do &quot;western&quot; WoD. I find it a bag full of shit in WoD.<br /> <br /> But lets go ahead. I never read Combat, but if it try to blend in any way SF and WoD, that stinks a lot. And I DO like SFRPG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T15:46:27-07:00","id":596224,"title":"","content":"Mage is also about transcendance. About comprehending your limits and going beyond them, and how you can choose to be tied by the petty and stupid things or become something special. I assume you don't like that either? Even in Werewolf you are actually holy warriors that serve entities such as these whose power over the cosmos is paramount and whose wisdom is boundless. Better yet, you progress through becoming the epitome of a cultural hero, becoming more legend than man. And let's not even start on Changeling.<br /> <br /> Just because you like something in WoD does not mean that's everything there is in the WoD. It's an insane hodepodge kitchensink and that's what's given it it's varied appeal and wide player base. Nota bene, I don't touch Vampire or Demon with a six foot pole, and that should tell you something about what I like in WoD.<br /> <br /> Just because we don't agree on what we like doesn't mean the other's games need to be excised with fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T15:48:51-07:00","id":596226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=596120#post596120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they are way beyond such paltry concerns as being Gods among men. They are the enlightened beings whose actual existence and power is predicated on being beyond trivial matters and embracing some pretty damn odd values. They are there to help others along the path, not indulge in petty temporal things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lovely and flowery, but not really relevant to any part of the quoted conversation. I'll bite anyway.<br /> <br /> If this is true, then what they clearly <i>aren't</i> doing is scaring those &quot;weak and petty antediluvians&quot; into hiding world-wide...<br /> <br /> Well, except when one wakes up in their back yard. Then they need to send <i>three of their eldest</i> after him and, best case scenario, <i>lose two before the third can deliver the killing blow</i> against the <i>freshly awakened</i> antediluvian, or worse case scenario they just get killed by the bomb that weakened said freshly awakened antediluvian.<br /> <br /> So, other than establishing that the Kuei-Jin <i>aren't</i> keeping the Antediluvians in check in any way at all (well, except waking up in their back yards, of course), and that they barely win best case scenario when three of their eldest go toe-to-toe with an Ante waking up from the world's longest nap, how are they proof the antediluvians aren't powerful blood-gods? Or more powerful than the Antes?<br /> <br /> Y'know, what the argument's about, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T21:31:38-07:00","id":596486,"title":"","content":"So many bad books...so many...<br /> <br /> I really want to say for anyone just aching for a copy of <b>Dark Reflections: Spectres</b>...it's honestly a really shitty book. It's not up there with some of the ones listed here...but it's really weak for what should have been a critical supplement on the major antagonists.<br /> <br /> Almost every general player's guide is a hodgepodge of terrible material and good stuff as well. The Technocracy Player's Guide and Shadow's Player's Guide are great as specific PGs, but the base Wraith and Mage Player's Guides are just incredibly random.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T00:32:46-07:00","id":596579,"title":"","content":"<i>Tribebook: CoG Revised </i>has already been mentioned as being one of the worst supplements of the cWoD, and I agree that <i>Gypsies </i>is without doubt the worst WW book ever published. I haven't read it and never want to, so I can't comment on its quality directly. Even so, the entire concept of the book should never have gotten off the brainstorming page. And <i>WoD: Mafia</i>? Same thing. Way too many stereotypes involved in either book to make it a practical gaming book.<br /> <br /> So those are my top three contenders for worst WW books ever published: 1. <i>Gypsies</i>, 2. <i>CoG Revised</i> and 3. <i>Mafia</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand</i> I remember enjoying when it first came out, but not long after that, I remember thinking how it was silly and over the top. And the stuff about Vicissitude being a sentient disease and the Souleater war I never liked at all. I'm interested to see how V20 will &quot;redeem&quot;(another poster's word, not mine) DSotBH in its future supplement, but that's for another thread and time.<br /> <br /> One particular book that I absolutely cannot stand (regardless of any quality as a gaming book it might have) is the Werewolf supplement <i>Chronicle of the Black Labyrinth</i>. When I bought it, I was expecting something like a Werewolf version of the Book of Nod. What I got was first-hand witness accounts of Wyrm-ridden perversities and atrocities that began turning my stomach from page 1. Granted, that's what the book is <i>supposed </i>to do, but to this day and for the rest of my life I absolutely refuse to take that book off my shelf nor remove it from its plastic storage bag. I mean, holy jeebus, even <i>Freak Legion</i> didn't gross me out as much. (Granted, <i>Freak Legion</i> had its own irreverent quality which took out some of the sting, but we all know that it's by no means a pleasant book to read.)<br /> <br /> People were actually hating on <i>Blood-Dimmed Tides</i>? I think that one is actually one of the best WW books of all. I wasn't much interested in the Changeling or Wraith parts of it, but the rest I liked. Hell, the blurb about the Arctic Ocean helped me find the Fifth Talon of the Wyrm!<br /> <br /> I'm not a big fan of Wraith, but I think WW went above and beyond the call of duty in trying to make <i>Shoah: Charnel Houses of Europe</i> as respectful of the Holocaust as they could. Hell, the foreword of <i>Shoah </i>even describes how the authors approached Janet Berliner to do the foreword for the book and how she almost balked at the idea of a gaming book using the Holocaust as setting until she said to herself &quot;We must teach them through the tools with which they are comfortable.&quot; Say what you will about the book, but the intentions of publishing it were honorable. I learned quite a bit about the Holocaust from this book, perhaps more than from any other source I've encountered in my life with the exception of the Holocaust Museum in DC. I'm just a short drive away from the Museum and my sister works there, too.<br /> <br /> (If you've never been to the Holocaust Museum in DC and get the opportunity to visit it, I emphatically recommend that you do so. Be warned, though: it's a <i>very</i> intense experience and not for the faint-hearted.)<br /> <br /> 1e Clanbook: Malkavian...perhaps the book most responsible for the proliferation of Fishmalk PCs. I tried to read that book and...couldn't. It gave one of my Vampire players a noteworthy character concept: an elder Noddist scholar who could very well have been a Mnemosyne...but the PC was still essentially a Fishmalk. Ugh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 07-20-2015, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T02:16:32-07:00","id":596596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=596226#post596226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lovely and flowery, but not really relevant to any part of the quoted conversation. I'll bite anyway.<br /> <br /> If this is true, then what they clearly <i>aren't</i> doing is scaring those &quot;weak and petty antediluvians&quot; into hiding world-wide...<br /> <br /> Well, except when one wakes up in their back yard. Then they need to send <i>three of their eldest</i> after him and, best case scenario, <i>lose two before the third can deliver the killing blow</i> against the <i>freshly awakened</i> antediluvian, or worse case scenario they just get killed by the bomb that weakened said freshly awakened antediluvian.<br /> <br /> So, other than establishing that the Kuei-Jin <i>aren't</i> keeping the Antediluvians in check in any way at all (well, except waking up in their back yards, of course), and that they barely win best case scenario when three of their eldest go toe-to-toe with an Ante waking up from the world's longest nap, how are they proof the antediluvians aren't powerful blood-gods? Or more powerful than the Antes?<br /> <br /> Y'know, what the argument's about, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>My comment wholly stems from the question of why the Kuei Jin aren't ruling as blood gods. The theoretical Dharma 9 (at 10 he's out of the game) bodhisattva is as powerful as an Antedelluvian. Mind you, he's probably completley uninterested in worldly affairs, making his game effect rather moot. The ones they sent were in the 7-8 Dharma range which puts them on the level of 4th or 5th gens. The conclusion of the Week of Nightmares wasn't that the Cathayans lost three Antedelluvian equivalents, but that they lost three powerful elders, which is quite a different tone.<br /> <br /> We also know that the Antedelluvians got eaten by their own children (reputably) and that it worked just fine. They are stupidly powerful, but that doesn't make them unstoppable.<br /> <br /> I was just saying why the Kuei Jin don't give a fuck about antes that aren't directly messing with them and theirs.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T02:47:42-07:00","id":596654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=595775#post595775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's already plenty of damn good reasons: each other, mortals bringing about Inquisition 2.0, Caine himself, torpor, and of course all the younglings rising up to hold Anarch Revolt Revised and do to them what was done to [Tzimisce] and [Lasombra] (supposedly, I know). You don't need to add fear of archmages and kuei-jin to the mix to make it plausible when they have plenty of plausible reasons for choosing a behind-the-scenes approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you need archmages and godlike KJ to even hurt them then a bunch of mortals rising up and doing Inqusition 2 is a joke to blood gods. Its a joke that a the anarchs will rise their way to the top and so on and so forth. That's my point. If they are in a &quot;Gods only apply&quot; level of power then the whole war of ages, the whole curse from caine that childe shall slay sire is a JOKE.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or to put it simply, the KJ elders did the sane reasonable setting thing when a nuke was dropped on them. They died. That means mortals can hurt them. The fact that Antedeluvian took the most powerful weapon mortals can make, shrugged it off and needed explicit technomagic shenanigans says &quot;no mortals can't do shit to him&quot;<br /> <br /> Now lets look at the rough power level of the KJ lets say they are roughly on par with a fourth gen vampire. So for the whole &quot;War of ages&quot; to matter we should assume one fourth gen should have a good chance of taking down a 3rd gen. 3 should have almost no problem... Seeing the problem with the Blood god Antedeluvians yet?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 07-20-2015, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T03:36:37-07:00","id":596677,"title":"","content":"Given the intent both of V20 and of DSotBH, I doubt it will be redeemed, to begin with. The content of the book will be alluded in a book about the Sabbat, and that's pretty much where it will end.<br /> <br /> The reason? Well, V20 is all about giving every rule needed to update any part of the game, and nothing about exploring the setting or giving way to the metaplot. DSotBH are all about the metaplot and the description of a conspiracy of EVUL VAMPS!<br /> <br /> I can't say I'm against it. I don't think Vampire Hero as a forbbiden concept, if you like it. But I can't see those two intents coming to terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T06:15:21-07:00","id":596810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=596654#post596654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you need archmages and godlike KJ to even hurt them then a bunch of mortals rising up and doing Inqusition 2 is a joke to blood gods. Its a joke that a the anarchs will rise their way to the top and so on and so forth. That's my point. If they are in a &quot;Gods only apply&quot; level of power then the whole war of ages, the whole curse from caine that childe shall slay sire is a JOKE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, once again, we've seen that those Anarchs can slay their sires (3rd generation). It might require a few of them, and they might need to catch the ante off-guard, but it can be done. Which, if you think about it, is pretty mythic. Zeus slew his father by catching him at the right moment. Other... Gods have slain other powerful deities (my brain isn't fully functioning yet to provide more examples, but they're out there).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=596654#post596654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or to put it simply, the KJ elders did the sane reasonable setting thing when a nuke was dropped on them. They died. That means mortals can hurt them. The fact that Antedeluvian took the most powerful weapon mortals can make, shrugged it off and needed explicit technomagic shenanigans says &quot;no mortals can't do shit to him&quot;<br /> <br /> Now lets look at the rough power level of the KJ lets say they are roughly on par with a fourth gen vampire. So for the whole &quot;War of ages&quot; to matter we should assume one fourth gen should have a good chance of taking down a 3rd gen. 3 should have almost no problem... Seeing the problem with the Blood god Antedeluvians yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't need to assume a single 4th gen needs to have a chance in a one-on-one, stand-up fight for the War of Ages to matter, because the War of Ages was never about Street Fighter-style battles to the death. It's about playing the long game to win. That's what the whole thing IS! Wheels within wheels, pawns moving pawns who move other pawns. Because when you are one of the thirteen blood gods, fighting any number of blood demigods you sired through the ages, you don't need to poke your head out there to win, but poking your head out there definitely allows your enemies to dog-pile on you.<br /> <br /> So no, we don't need to assume a single 4th gen can take on a 3rd gen. And coincidentally, we don't see that happening. We see three Bodhisattva are needed for one freshly awakened Ante. We see Tremere taking down a sleeping ante, and still bringing pals along just in case. We see a band of allies going after [Lasombra] and [Tzimisce], and only getting one of those two dead (and he might have even been willing, so yeah).<br /> <br /> The problem I do see, however, is if a single 4th gen can take on a 3rd gen in a straight fight and have even a &quot;less than 50%, but better than 33%&quot; chance of winning, then the War of Ages starts making no sense. Because there are a hell of a lot more 4th generation kindred than there are 3rd gen. How have so many antediluvians survived into the modern age if they are outnumbered by guys with a good chance of taking them down and a motivation to do so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T06:28:42-07:00","id":596815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=596677#post596677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the intent both of V20 and of DSotBH, I doubt it will be redeemed, to begin with. The content of the book will be alluded in a book about the Sabbat, and that's pretty much where it will end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, the Tal'Mah'Re is officially getting a v20 book. It has been announced and is in the development process.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T08:44:10-07:00","id":597015,"title":"","content":"Nice. In that case, I have no idea what they're going to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T10:54:32-07:00","id":597070,"title":"","content":"I would like to toss in &quot;<b>Holy War</b>,&quot; from Hunter: the Reckoning. It had some really cool stuff in it (a Hunter-Net equivalent for regions with limited internet access, nifty new Edges, and a good... attempt... at a non-Western outlook on The Hunt), but it also had some very silly things (Middle-Eastern Imbued can't be Martyrs, because Islam encourages <i>everyone</i> to sacrifice themselves for the good of others).<br /> <br /> Now, White Wolf isn't entirely to blame for the awkwardness of this book, considering that it was published one week before September 11th, 2001. Had the terrorist attacks not occurred, it would have just been one more RPG setting book that plays up outdated stereotypes for the sake of an exotic setting. But afterwards... the outdated stereotypes and politics just became uncomfortable and obviously inaccurate.<br /> <br /> Although, if they had written and published it a year later, it might have been far worse...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:24:01-07:00","id":597089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=596654#post596654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you need archmages and godlike KJ to even hurt them then a bunch of mortals rising up and doing Inqusition 2 is a joke to blood gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Historically the Inquisition has made use of vampires' own weaknesses to level the playing field: their vulnerability to fire, sunlight, and the power of religious faith. So the mortals are getting help from a god considerably bigger than the blood gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T12:05:01-07:00","id":597130,"title":"","content":"i've always been under the impression that it has more to do with the raw power of their own faith and convictions rather than any higher power. I've heard stories of people with faith in capitalism holding off vampires with credit cards before. <br /> <br /> <br /> back to the subject.<br /> <br /> I'd have to say that the worst is Gypsies just on sheer prinicpal, but in all honesty I was really really disappointed with Gehenna. all of the scenerios were kind of &quot;Hey watch the NPCs have all the fun!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T14:20:32-07:00","id":597315,"title":"","content":"Whenever I see this sort of post, I always wish the OP would say something to the effect of &quot;...besides/other than <i>Gypsies</i>&quot;, or even more broadly, &quot;what are the worst books for reasons besides their problematic representations of one or more human cultures or societies?&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously, we get it, no one here is a racist--racists and racism are bad; real Gypsies are a nuanced human culture that should probably not have been &quot;splatted&quot; for the purposes of an RPG. But it's almost as if people mention the Gypsies book as an introductory paragraph before they get into discussing what is almost certainly more useful or interesting to OP: books the content of which was not systematically or narratively useful or interesting. Poorly written books (in the sense that they're hard to follow, poorly organized, boring, what have you).<br /> <br /> EDIT: <i>WOD: Mafia</i> is hot garbage--just boring and devoid of interesting material. I also never enjoyed <i>Tradition Book: Cult of Ecstasy (Rev.)</i> though I've had this discussion enough to know that few (if any) people share that sentiment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 07-20-2015, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T16:28:02-07:00","id":597484,"title":"","content":"The thing with Gypsies isn't just for being a prejudice-produced piece of shit. Its for being the major one, and that means precisely that as much as prejudice it have the other characteristics of very bad writen book.<br /> <br /> But yeah, we realy have to go past prejudice, it isn't the point here.<br /> <br /> From the Time of Judgement books... well, yeah, Gehenna was kind of less than it could be, but I hardly would consider it the worst. The scenario ideas are good, just need some thinkering to deliver more power in the PCs hands, and te book as a whole does a reasonable job to help the ST.<br /> <br /> I found Ascension, tough, to be the worst. First, it delivered something that wasn't supposed to be delivered in those books: an official end. That sucked a lot, not because is a bad ending, but because it takes most of the book, becomes kind of boring in some points for being too long, and them forces the alternatives to be shortened.<br /> <br /> Ascension was the worst, by far, IMHO. Gehenna was ok for me, Apocalypse and Time of Judgement even better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T19:02:27-07:00","id":597651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=597315#post597315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I also never enjoyed <i>Tradition Book: Cult of Ecstasy (Rev.)</i> though I've had this discussion enough to know that few (if any) people share that sentiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, what did you have problems with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T19:03:09-07:00","id":597656,"title":"","content":"How on earth has nobody mentioned Chaos Factor?<br /> <br /> You've got Sammy H. You've got terrible crossover mechanics. You have Shaitan and all the awfulness his background implies (He and Gangrel are the childer of the same Antediluvian?! And Ashur's entire batch of childer except Gangrel were corrupted by Shai-Shai?? There's just so much badness here I can't even. I just can't.)<br /> <br /> I am going to assume people have just retconned it from their own memories of terribadliness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T19:07:23-07:00","id":597666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=597656#post597656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How on earth has nobody mentioned Chaos Factor?<br /> <br /> You've got Sammy H. You've got terrible crossover mechanics. You have Shaitan and all the awfulness his background implies (He and Gangrel are the childer of the same Antediluvian?! And Ashur's entire batch of childer except Gangrel were corrupted by Shai-Shai?? There's just so much badness here I can't even. I just can't.)<br /> <br /> I am going to assume people have just retconned it from their own memories of terribadliness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to mention it and everything that Sam had been in after VF, but got side-tracked by another topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T23:50:15-07:00","id":597977,"title":"","content":"By the way, we could gave a Honor Trophy to Samuel Height. Isn't a book, but the guy is the very stuff of legendary badliness.<br /> <br /> I remember now half-human, half-garou, half-vampire, half-mage. Any other half he achieved before entirely ashtray?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T01:37:19-07:00","id":598058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=597015#post597015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice. In that case, I have no idea what they're going to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>They'll be the True Black Hand from The Vampire Storyteller's Handbook. Which worked more or less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T09:49:34-07:00","id":598455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=597656#post597656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How on earth has nobody mentioned Chaos Factor?<br /> <br /> You've got Sammy H. You've got terrible crossover mechanics. You have Shaitan and all the awfulness his background implies (He and Gangrel are the childer of the same Antediluvian?! And Ashur's entire batch of childer except Gangrel were corrupted by Shai-Shai?? There's just so much badness here I can't even. I just can't.)<br /> <br /> I am going to assume people have just retconned it from their own memories of terribadliness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>looooooove</i> that book--it is so completely bananas that I can't help but enjoy it. I basically like that book for the same reason I enjoy the movies <i>Crank </i>and <i>Crank 2: High Voltage</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T10:15:21-07:00","id":598480,"title":"","content":"Sure, Gypsie was bad, but look at the State of Grace or, worst, Chaining the Beast. They add nothing to the setting, repeating old stuff, and the writing is... quite uninspired. They made me wanting the end of V:tM back then...<br /> <br /> Rage Across Australia for Werewolf : for the many reason may of you pointed out. And yes, Children of Gaia Rev. was also abysmal.<br /> <br /> The Book of World for Mage : seriously, does someone really understood something the first time he read it ? So much mumbo jumbo. And Mage's umbra is an utter mess since.<br /> <br /> Hunter : Utopia : a book about &quot;what if hunter wins&quot;. For a 96 page sourcebook, only 3 pages are about that, and it is kind of : &quot;make stuff up!&quot; followed by : &quot;and don't forget there is even bigger monsters&quot; Seriously, I've just pay 15$ ish buck for THAT !?!!?<br /> <br /> I think KOTE wasn't that bad, but WW had fallen in the trap of exoticism : it is good because it isn't Western (In some was, the same can be said about Gypsie). But there is still potential if KOTE, Blood and Silk was infinitly better and the world building was greath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2140-asimar","name":"Asimar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T12:39:32-07:00","id":598623,"title":"","content":"Near the top of my personal list is <i>Time of Thin Blood</i>. Well, actually, most of it is OK until we get to the Week of Nightmares - which is bad enough to tarnish the rest of the book. The entire fight with Ravnos waking up and the gonzo way he's destroyed seems more appropriate for <i>Rifts</i> than V:tM. At least <i>Gypsies</i> can be easily ignored, but the Week of Nightmares became canon and affected everything following it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 07-21-2015, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T14:22:33-07:00","id":598672,"title":"","content":"In that regard, I wouldn't count the Week of Nightmares as part of ToTB per se. It was more the Thing Already Planned to Begin Everyone's End Times, and ToTB was just the selected book to put this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T15:21:27-07:00","id":598719,"title":"","content":"<i>Wod: Mafia</i> was not terrible, but it also wasn't good either. Very dry. But I have a specific complaint about it. Ignore the stereotypes, ignore how it deliberately went for a more Sopranos/Godfather feel. My problem was that it was a Sicilian Mafia book, when it should have been an Organized Crime book. What if I want to include stuff about the Russian mob? The South American Cartels? The Triads or Tongs? The Yakuza? Even just the average, street level gangs? <i>WoD: Mafia</i> gives me no help, save for a few pages near the end talking about how the Mafia interacts with them.<br /> <br /> This is especially galling because organized crime is a key facet of the World of Darkness. Many of the splats - Vampires, Kuei-Jin, Mages, Werewolves - exist in a world outside the law. Kindred can't exist without at least regularly committing assault and/or fraud, among many other crimes to make their unlives easier. Same with Kuei-Jin, who get most of their Chi from people's blood. Garou actively engage in corporate espionage and environmental terrorism in their fight against the Wyrm. Tradition Mages actively stay under the radar to avoid the Technocracy, who themselves have agents infiltrating many strata of society, including organized crime. Hunters are basically armed cells waging a private war against &quot;monsters&quot;, and need heavy ordinance to fight that war. And you bet your ass crime produces more than its fair share of Wraiths. The only reason Changelings have no hand in crime is because most of them go into banality-induced hibernation for the rest of their mortal lives at some point during childhood or adolescence. And Demons? Well, make your own connections.<br /> <br /> And yet there's no book specifically about organized crime, and how it fits into a world with all these supernaturals. We have a book about government agents (<i>Project Twilight</i>, a decent book I think), but the best we get is <i>WoD: Mafia</i> in terms of crime. A book that covers only a fraction of organized crime, and then only a heavily stylized version of it. If nothing else, I want a WoD book about organized crime because existing and working outside the law applies to both criminals and the supernatural splats. Thematically, tonally, the two are made for each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T00:47:45-07:00","id":599074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asimar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=598480#post598480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Book of World for Mage : seriously, does someone really understood something the first time he read it ? So much mumbo jumbo. And Mage's umbra is an utter mess since.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? Really? That thing is AMAZING! It's got material for at least a thousand different stories! What was so confusing for you?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T10:12:15-07:00","id":599596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=599074#post599074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, what? Really? That thing is AMAZING! It's got material for at least a thousand different stories! What was so confusing for you?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Book of World is quite a good source of inspiration, but its editing, the way matter is presented in the book, is, IMHO, the worst of the White-Wolf era (and that, considering the way many of these books require you to do back and forth, searching in pages XX, that's saying something). I was quite confused the first time I've read it, and the second time, and I've begun to understand a bit the third... and again until I finally get it entirely ! <br /> With hindsight, I'll said that the writers wanted it to be a bit &quot;trippy&quot;, so I guest it wasn't really my style.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2140-asimar","name":"Asimar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T22:52:51-07:00","id":600204,"title":"","content":"One thing can be said: WW was really bad in organizing information on the books. They WHERE meant to be read front-to-back, and information that should be together where scattered througout the books. Vampire Core is a prime exemple of this worse than bad organization, whyle Demon is almost good.<br /> <br /> The first time I saw Requiem: Blood &amp; Smoke index, I almost cried of pure happiness...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T03:24:54-07:00","id":600314,"title":"","content":"The Worst games in Classic World Of Darkness? This is just my opinion but they may be:<br /> <br /> 1) Mummy The Resurrection: For what I know, a newborn mummy is nothing else than a rotting zombie at begins. To complete its transformation, the mummy need to travel to the middle east which is not exactly behind the corner! I feel poorly realistic that a undead body may undertake a such long journey without attract any attention. Moreover, mummes goes out of energy if they leave the middle east and I find this a nasty limitation.<br /> <br /> 2) Changeling the Dreaming: I've read something about it. Using their own fantasy and imagination, changelings can transform broomsticks into legendary weapons and themseves into fairy tales' beings like orcs or elves. However, if a mere human happens to be witness to a duel between changelings, he will not see two fairy beings fighting with their mistical swords, but just two people who helds broomsticks pretending to be shining knights. I feel quite unactrattive to play characters which basically are affected by Peter Pan's Syndrome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 07-23-2015, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T09:57:49-07:00","id":600647,"title":"","content":"I try not to think of Chaos Factor the former super being that is now an ashtray ranks extremely high on my personal hate list.<br /> <br /> World of Darkness Mafia: I didn't mind this as much as some of the others, yes it was to focused on the Sicilian mafia but the Sicilian mafia is what most people think of when they hear organized crime. <br /> I wouldn't mind seeing a better book on Organized Crime covering the whole world.<br /> <br /> Combat sigh so much potential so little use...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T13:44:38-07:00","id":602235,"title":"","content":"Caerns, Places of Power-While not awfully terrible, the book has less details on Caerns than Players Guide to Garou. Not really good for a -Caern- book. But what makes it terrible is the metis section. While it has a -lot- of good info, it is shadowed by a narrator who manages to be whiny and non-sensical. Most of its metis focused merits or flaws are essentially fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T23:25:50-07:00","id":602615,"title":"","content":"I think you are mixing up the Caerns: Places of Power book and Guardians of the Caerns. The first one is just a long list of funky Garou places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T03:54:10-07:00","id":602773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=602615#post602615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are mixing up the Caerns: Places of Power book and Guardians of the Caerns. The first one is just a long list of funky Garou places.</div> </div> </div> </div>..Yeah, I am. Guardians of the Caerns was the book x.x","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T14:14:41-07:00","id":603188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=602235#post602235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guardians of the Caerns -- While not awfully terrible, the book has less details on Caerns than Players Guide to Garou. Not really good for a -Caern- book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're crazy. Guardians has 70+ pages of information (I'm not counting the metis chapter in this page count) on caerns and their infrastructure, defenses, etc. while Players Guide to Garou only has 20 pages. You can't tell me that 70 is less than 20. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=602235#post602235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what makes it terrible is the metis section. While it has a -lot- of good info, it is shadowed by a narrator who manages to be whiny and non-sensical. Most of its metis focused merits or flaws are essentially fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>A metis being &quot;whiny&quot; about being treated like a second-class citizen over his birth, something he's not even responsible for? Gaia preserve us, how could such a thing ever come to pass? Snark aside, this sounds perfectly in-character to me. It doesn't strike me as nonsensical at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T14:57:29-07:00","id":603223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=603188#post603188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're crazy. Guardians has 70+ pages of information (I'm not counting the metis chapter in this page count) on caerns and their infrastructure, defenses, etc. while Players Guide to Garou only has 20 pages. You can't tell me that 70 is less than 20. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A metis being &quot;whiny&quot; about being treated like a second-class citizen over his birth, something he's not even responsible for? Gaia preserve us, how could such a thing ever come to pass? Snark aside, this sounds perfectly in-character to me. It doesn't strike me as nonsensical at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I was too harsh on the Caern point.<br /> <br /> As for the metis, it isn't that the narrator is bitter about things. It's that at one point this Athro Galliard Child of Gaia says that he gets his wounds treated last and unless his packmates call for him to speak during moots, he doesn't get a turn. I admit this is entirely based on the games I've played, but once a metis hits Athro, their rank should pretty much makes those things pretty hard to do. But, I admit its based on personal gaming experiences here ^^''","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T15:29:07-07:00","id":603249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=603223#post603223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit I was too harsh on the Caern point.<br /> <br /> As for the metis, it isn't that the narrator is bitter about things. It's that at one point this Athro Galliard Child of Gaia says that he gets his wounds treated last and unless his packmates call for him to speak during moots, he doesn't get a turn. I admit this is entirely based on the games I've played, but once a metis hits Athro, their rank should pretty much makes those things pretty hard to do. But, I admit its based on personal gaming experiences here ^^''</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, a Rank 4/Athro metis of the <i>Children of Gaia </i>is complaining of unfair and unequal treatment? Ok, yeah, that does sound nonsensical. Granted, even some of the CoGs can be assholes; even Sam Haight got his Start of Darkness because he was abused by his CoG Garou father. But an Athro, being that high-ranked, still getting abused by his own CoG pack? Yeah, that <i>does </i>kinda ring false. Not ringing false in that the metis is being whiny, but ringing false that his packmates (who are likely of equal rank with him) wouldn't know better than to abuse a Garou of such stature. Especially since the CoGs are the tribe that specifically accept metis from the other tribes.<br /> <br /> Ok, Ana, now I agree with you.<br /> <br /> Man, why do the CoGs get so short-changed in how people try to describe them? CoG Revised got them all wrong and now whoever wrote this in-character metis CoG got the CoGs wrong <i>again</i>. Doesn't <i>anybody </i>truly get the CoGs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 07-25-2015, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T16:10:36-07:00","id":603267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=603249#post603249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, a Rank 4/Athro metis of the <i>Children of Gaia </i>is complaining of unfair and unequal treatment? Ok, yeah, that does sound nonsensical. Granted, even some of the CoGs can be assholes; even Sam Haight got his Start of Darkness because he was abused by his CoG Garou father. But an Athro, being that high-ranked, still getting abused by his own CoG pack? Yeah, that <i>does </i>kinda ring false. Not ringing false in that the metis is being whiny, but ringing false that his packmates (who are likely of equal rank with him) wouldn't know better than to abuse a Garou of such stature. Especially since the CoGs are the tribe that specifically accept metis from the other tribes.<br /> <br /> Ok, Ana, now I agree with you.<br /> <br /> Man, why do the CoGs get so short-changed in how people try to describe them? CoG Revised got them all wrong and now whoever wrote this in-character metis CoG got the CoGs wrong <i>again</i>. Doesn't <i>anybody </i>truly get the CoGs?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was more in terms of others outside his pack doing that. But it isn't said they were out of the tribe, either. As in, this <i>Athro Galliard </i>cannot tell a story during a moot at all unless his packmates basically ask others to let him. And the pack's ragabash's kills are noted more than this guy's? Again, Athro. As in, most likely higher rank than some healers/the Talesinger.<br /> <br /> At that point, even if it is a metis, it is still higher ranked than you. I just can't imagine a Child of Gaia sept doing this shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T20:45:42-07:00","id":603440,"title":"","content":"I can't see ANYONE but some, SOME, Get or Fang doing this shit. When the guy is Rank 4 it is pretty much YOUR turn to whine if don't like him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T21:58:06-07:00","id":603494,"title":"","content":"If we've progressed down from &quot;the worst&quot; to &quot;serious issues, but not that bad&quot;, I'm going to nominate Blood and Silk for its bizarre fixation on making the Hakken out to be the only Garou in the Beast Courts, naming Chi You as one of them, and that sidebar in the initial overview chapter that conflated Yale Romanization of Mandarin with Legge. Said sidebar then went on to claim that Blood and Silk would be using Hanyu Pinyin Romanization, which is a lie so grave that its back cover should have set itself aflame spontaneously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T00:32:25-07:00","id":603590,"title":"","content":"well, that's just it. he's Athro... but he's still crap. In a tribe that is known for &quot;treating metis better.&quot; 'Cause for all their talk, end of the day the children of gaia <i>are</i> creatures of rage and instinct and theocratic tradition. The metis are <i>wrong</i>, the Litany is what it is, and the children of gaia are just as known for <i>not</i> living up to their own standards. So yeah, even the &quot;best option&quot; for a metis is going to be pretty lame, 'cause he's a metis. Flip side of the coin is the &quot;too helpful&quot; approach, a bunch of Gaians or Glass Walkers wanting to make <i>themselves</i> feel better by fawning over the metis like a child with a new puppy.<br /> <br /> anyway...<br /> <br /> <b>Denizens of the dreaming:</b> I swear that like, half of this book's content was in the form of web-published errata. And it's still not clear to me, <i>after all these years</i> how the Adhene are supposed to &quot;work.&quot; I mean, i get the gist of it, but it seems they had a bunch of ideas for &quot;doing changeling different&quot; and just hodgepodged it all onto the Adhene. <br /> <br /> <b>Bygone bestiary:</b> Speaking of halfassed products...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T07:53:55-07:00","id":603803,"title":"","content":"While the Garou can be stuck up bastards, they are a quite eglaitarian society once Renown gets into it. A character who colelcted all the Renown and challenged all the characters he had to to get Rank 4 is a legend. Some people will talk bad stuff behind his back, but no one in his right mind will deny him his, because he will be more then able to take it by force and the weight of his persona.<br /> <br /> Bygone Bestiary isn't bad. The monsters in it are totally cool. I got no idea why people seem so fixated on playable monsters and the fact that the system for them is a bit limiting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T11:12:38-07:00","id":603966,"title":"","content":"Just to add a little thing to the Athro question, a Metis probably had to do MORE THAN enough to achieve Rank 5 just to achieve Rank 4. Either way, once Athro, Athro he is. It IS like a military rank, he just CAN'T be ignored without dyre consequences.<br /> <br /> If he complained about not being Rank 5 yet, then it would probably make sense. Even for a Rank 3 Metis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T12:34:02-07:00","id":604014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592883-what-are-the-worst-classic-wod-sourcebooks-in-your-opinion?p=603966#post603966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to add a little thing to the Athro question, a Metis probably had to do MORE THAN enough to achieve Rank 5 just to achieve Rank 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that is how renown works. Metis do not suffer penalties to renown, and unless whoever is issuing the rank challenges is intentionally trying to sabotage the Garou in question, the spirits will recognize that the Garou is worthy. There is also pretty huge difference between the higher ranks. What is required of an athro versus and Elder is substantial, as is the difference between an Elder and a Legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}